  "gaps": [
    "The program table gives only a combined 48-credit block for remaining general education and electives; it does not state how those 48 credits split between remaining general education categories and free electives. The general education framework totals 41 credits (Communications 12, Mathematics 3, Arts and Humanities 6, Behavioral and Social Sciences 6, Biological and Physical Sciences 7, Research and Computing Literacy 7). The catalog says 15 business core credits (CIFS 300, ECON 201, ECON 203, STAT 200, WRTG 112) 'may be applied to general education requirements'. However, the capture does not explicitly state the resulting remaining general education credits or the elective remainder.",
    "Residency is stated only at the degree level, not per course: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30) must be completed at UMGC; half the credits within the major must be completed at UMGC; at least 15 upper-level credits (300–499) must be completed at UMGC. The capture does not say which specific courses must be taken at UMGC.",
    "Credits for the alternate course options (e.g., BMGT 382, WDDE 305, BMGT 110, BMGT 365, BMGT 381) are not printed separately; they are assumed to satisfy the same 3-credit slot.",
    "Grade rules affecting transfer applicability are stated but are not per-requirement ledger items: minimum grade C for any course applied to the major; WRTG 112 requires C- or better within the first 24 credits and may not be earned through Prior Learning; at least half of major credits must be graded coursework."
  ],
